<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Princeton University</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1746">1746</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as College of New Jersey</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Princeton University is a private university in Princeton, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-jersey">New Jersey</a>, chartered in 1746 as the College of New Jersey, the fourth college founded in British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>. It moved to Princeton in 1756, where its Nassau Hall briefly housed the Congress of the Confederation in 1783. It took its present name in 1896.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/princeton-university.jpg" alt="Princeton University" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original author unknown. The shield was described in an 1896 minutes of the meeting · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Princeton_seal.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
